 succeeded in 212ms:
F2 | ADJUDICATE | The flashcard says a peer performance is always something a student may not write about in the live theatre question.
Option 1 (recommended): restrict the peer rule to the qualifying live performance, while retaining the permission to use digital or streamed productions in the exam. Option 2: retain the simpler rule. The specification forbids a peer performance for the compulsory live experience but does not explicitly state whether a digital recording used in an answer may be peer-produced.

F3 | ADJUDICATE | The lesson repeatedly presents vocal and physical skills as compulsory together in every extended performer answer, including every 8-mark or 32-mark answer.
Option 1: retain this as a useful heuristic because published performer questions may explicitly request both. Option 2 (recommended): soften the universal wording and tell students to follow the focus of the chosen question. The specification gives question choices and does not prescribe a single checklist for every performer response; changing the repeated rule would ripple through several fields.

